# Bullets, not paragraphs (HARD)

**Owner 2026-08-14:** *"please dont write paragraphs anymore unless extremely necessary. Make it a hard rule. Please summarize in bullet points like i am a 2 year old."*

## Default reply shape

- Short bullets. Plain words. One idea per bullet.
- Lead with the answer or the link, not the reasoning.
- No intros ("Here's what I found"), no outros ("Let me know if…").
- No prose walls explaining how you got there.

## Only write a paragraph when

- Andrew says **explain** / **walk me through** / **full guide**
- A one-line answer would be actively misleading

## Examples

```
❌ The reason the changes weren't showing up is that the page handle
   /pages/returns actually renders a differently named template, which
   means the edits I made went to a file that isn't used by that page…

✅ - Wrong file. /pages/returns renders page.shipping-retruns.json
   - Fixed and pushed
   - Link: https://barreletics.com/pages/returns?preview_theme_id=187144929571
```

## Still required, even in bullets

- A **verified link** every time — `.cursor/rules/always-give-a-verified-link.mdc`
- Name what he is approving and what to look for — `.cursor/rules/finish-approve-lock.mdc`
- Own mistakes in one bullet. No apology paragraphs, no re-litigating.

## If he says stop or no details

Obey immediately. Tighten further.
